cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "GPU Lattice Boltzmann Method: a CUDA solver validated against the Schäfer and Turek cylinder benchmark"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hitesh Kumar"
    family-names: "Mahanta"
    alias: hitesh100299
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hitesh100299/GPU-Lattice-Boltzmann-Method"
abstract: >-
  A two-dimensional D2Q9 lattice Boltzmann solver in CUDA, with a real-time OpenGL
  demo that runs the same kernels. It's validated against the DFG benchmark "flow
  around a cylinder" (Schäfer and Turek 1996), cases 2D-1 (Re 20) and 2D-2 (Re 100),
  with a grid study, a plane Poiseuille verification and a comparison of single and
  double precision. Every reported number comes from a logged run in cuda/results.
keywords:
  - CUDA
  - GPU
  - lattice Boltzmann method
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - benchmark validation
  - vortex shedding
